## Novel Insights

The combination of condition-type-specific structural priors (diagonal for spatial, keyword-activated for subject) with decoupled self-attention groups that enable KV caching is a genuinely useful design pattern for multi-condition DiTs. The empirical finding that visual conditions exert their strongest influence at early (high-noise) denoising timesteps, validated through the perturbation SSIM analysis, has implications for fine-tuning strategy beyond the specific PKA architecture. However, the paper's failure to jointly evaluate efficiency and quality at the same condition counts means the most practically important result — whether the 10× speedup is achievable at deployment quality — remains empirically open.

